Title: F2-M06 — Red Tideworks (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. HARBOURMASTER'S OFFICE, COAST ROAD - DUSK

[[AMBIENCE: surf on a breakwater, pump machinery thudding in the distance, a foghorn]]
[[MUSIC: driving, industrial tension]]

A harbour chart is spread across a chart table under a swinging lamp. COMMANDER SAVA and PETROV stand over it. A stopwatch sits on the chart.

COMMANDER SAVA
(serious)
Fuel is moving through the coastal pumping station to vessels with no national markings. Command calls them Compact tankers. Nobody at Command has seen a hull.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: coast road running north-east from the base, dock landing and causeway, service works west of the station, tank farm and shore towers, control building, inlet with naval yard site, moored unmarked vessels]]

PETROV
(alert)
The transfer completes in eighteen minutes. Once the ships leave, we lose the trail.

PETROV
Coast road to the dock landing: three minutes for armour. A guard team and two towers at the landing, then the causeway straight to the control building. That is the short way.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
The risk is the short way. Operators who load unmarked ships do not leave their front door open. If the causeway goes, we turn back west and enter through the service works, and that costs time we do not have.

PETROV
The inlet below the station takes gunboats. The shore guns on the tank farm will sink them unless the depots are down first.

COMMANDER SAVA
(firm)
Capture the control room before the transfer ends. If the docks are scuttled, push inland through the service works.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
Whatever is written on those manifests, I want a copy before the station burns. I am done taking Command's word for who we are shooting at.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
